    "summary": "I built a compact desk unit from three hex bases at level 0: two full bases at (0,0) and (1,0), and a north-half base at (0,1). The three bases meet at one corner. A drawer sits on the cut face of the half base. At the shared corner there's a mount spike carrying a small platform. The first spike I placed was a solid one, and the configurator wouldn't let it carry a platform, so I swapped it for a mount spike. I then capped every open face (9 solid end caps) and bolted the joints (3 joint bolts). That makes 18 parts, at about 1264 g of filament and roughly 1833 minutes of printing. The final check found no rule issues and no mesh clashes. I didn't add any desk props, since you only asked for parts.",
